date: 2026-03-03T00:00:00-04:00
---

Anzu is a small, light bird-like man (a tengu) with feathers and a beak, and a member of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He is well-studied in occult and religious matters, keeps the raven [[People/Othello|Othello]], and comes from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], where much of his family is connected to [[Belvedere]]. He heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]].

He was the only survivor of the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and has since travelled with [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]], [[People/Johnny|Johnny Skyfall]] and [[People/Benny|Benny]].

In a Widdershins alley he killed the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], who had helped kill his friends. He pulled a coin from the fountain Hlarf was pissing in and sent it through his head. The Party kept Hlarf's car, a 632 Chorath Aventine.

In the fane beneath the Gas-n-Go he killed [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]], taking hold of the burnt husk's mind and making it drive its own body to move. It could not, and tore itself apart.

In the armory he identified the white armband and the two silver rings. In the ambush of the shift crew he kept his distance, and the werebear that swelled to fill the hall never reached him.

In [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Brooks]]'s flat he cast over the room and found the hidden [[Bestiary/Cairn White|cairn white]], and in the fight he named the [[Bestiary/Lovelorn|lovelorn]] heart-undead. He called out for Brooks and got no answer.

Before sleeping that night he turned his mind to the singer of the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] and said he saw now why the power had been given to him, that he saw the danger coming, and that he would save them; the song quickened for half a second before settling.

He bought heal scrolls from Arctos before the sale. At the cabin at void 26 Anaïs kicked him across the room when he came near the bed, and the shackle would not open for him, since he carries no mark of Aut. He showed Anaïs the address his sister had written to explain how the Party had found him.

With the pilgrimage two days off he forged three more invitations from the one the Party had stolen, matching its blue cardstock and gold ink closely enough that the real one could not be told from the copies, and bought a corduroy jacket for the party. At the rest-stop gas station on the way he knocked the cashier unconscious, and when he roused him afterward he warned him that he had known about the trap and that it would not have flown. He put a rock through the head of one of the robbers.

At the pilgrimage he took a blank white mask with nothing on it but eye slots, and it pressed over his beak without trouble. He held his place in the fortune teller's line with [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] while [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] and [[People/Benny|Benny]] went to the other path, and came over when Johnny told them it was gladiator combat.

At the train yard the wheel landed on red and three [[Bestiary/Barbazu|Barbazu]] and a [[Bestiary/Brimorak|Brimorak]] came out of the smoke. He read one devil, and told it its arms looked weak, and whether by luck or by the insult it was true and the words hurt it badly; Johnny piled on with the same insult. He drew on the song he had heard, saw his own arms come apart into tentacles and mouths, and reached out with his mind to strike at the devils at a distance. The brimorak's blood and sword put him on the ground, and his raven [[People/Othello|Othello]] spent itself to wake him. He healed Benny and Johnny where he could, and was on his feet and bleeding when it ended, though he stopped the bleeding on himself.

At the pilgrimage he stood in one of the three rings of the association game and put a scroll of invisibility in the overlap he shared with Johnny, and at the prism he worked the order of the seven potions out of the riddle and reached through the seven walls to pull out the key. He gave his name as Anzu Koreshi, academic fellow, to get the four of them into the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]], where he read on Archmechanics and searched the two artists' names.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]] he combed the reference shelves and then took a hand in the periodicals study the others had begun, looking for a pattern behind the Embercall and the fire cults. What he could put together was thin: around six months after the [[Voidsong]] was first heard, Teller's Run was walled in and a burst of fire cults appeared across [[Færrin]] and [[Geography/Velthara/index|Velthara]], then tapered off. He also learned, from an old Prime Meridian fluff piece, that the Org installed three great [[Phenomena/Hearts|Hearts]] to coordinate [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]'s transport about a century ago, one of them in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]; no record names Rapid Connection.

He asked after giant-kind and angels, and was told giants are thought to have a home Joker World but none live on [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], while angels are made by the Outer Gods to work on this world. At the [[Sin and Tonic]] he met the returned Marchal twins and traded hints on keystone 14, and he proposed the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|Hallia Metropolitan Conservatory]] as the place to find a painting worth the Heart's while.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|MetCon]] he read the paintings and the names on the plaques, and saw that the sculpture of the World Branch was a representation no scholar he knew of would make. He tipped the tour guide a gold piece. At 414 Anchor Street he fought from the air, tore the arm off a pusk with a telekinetic projectile, killed a mioktan and a pusk with a burst of force, and read Sbrtlby as a [[Bestiary/Babau|babau]], a demon that acid could not touch and that cold iron and holy things could.

Back at the bar he read what was taken off [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]]. The four triangles of yellow paper were fulus that fix a circle in which the Party goes unseen by one kind of creature; the three vials were doses of a suppressant that blunts an addiction, which he named only the next morning; the red choker was a choker of elocution, which lets its wearer speak the tongue of demons and went to [[People/Johnny|Johnny]]. At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] he read keystone 14 as a key to a sealed compartment of some kind, with something in it that only receives. In the lobby fight he threw [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]] into [[People/Benny|Benny]]'s reach.
